From 59ec25c514b43c5141ef97f3fb566baa2087bf50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:14:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bfd: microblaze: apply relocations the .eh_frame editor asks
 to keep static

When a shared object is linked, _bfd_elf_section_offset returns -2 for
an R_MICROBLAZE_32 in .eh_frame whose FDE the eh_frame editor is
converting to a PC-relative encoding: no dynamic relocation is wanted,
but the absolute value must be written into the section so that the
editor can turn it into a delta.  Every other backend handles that
case with "skip = true, relocate = true" and then applies the
relocation in place.  elf32-microblaze.c only skipped.  On a RELA
target the addend lives in the relocation, so the field kept its
assembled value of zero and _bfd_elf_write_section_eh_frame turned
that into a PC-relative pointer to address 0.

GCC-generated frames never hit this because GCC uses DW_EH_PE_aligned
for PIC MicroBlaze code, which the editor leaves alone (hence the
writable .eh_frame full of R_MICROBLAZE_REL relocations in every
MicroBlaze DSO).  Assembler-generated frames use the default sdata4
encoding and did hit it: with CFI directives in glibc's MicroBlaze
assembly, every one of those FDEs in libc.so covered pc=0..size.

bfd/ChangeLog:
	* elf32-microblaze.c (microblaze_elf_relocate_section): Apply the
	relocation statically when _bfd_elf_section_offset returns -2.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 bfd/elf32-microblaze.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bfd/elf32-microblaze.c b/bfd/elf32-microblaze.c
index 027b1886e9a..86429e772a4 100644
--- a/bfd/elf32-microblaze.c
+++ b/bfd/elf32-microblaze.c
@@ -1644,7 +1644,7 @@ microblaze_elf_relocate_section (struct bfd_link_info *info,
 		  {
 		    Elf_Internal_Rela outrel;
 		    bfd_byte *loc;
-		    bool skip;
+		    bool skip, relocate;
 
 		    /* When generating a shared object, these relocations
 		       are copied into the output file to be resolved at run
@@ -1653,6 +1653,7 @@ microblaze_elf_relocate_section (struct bfd_link_info *info,
 		    BFD_ASSERT (sreloc != NULL);
 
 		    skip = false;
+		    relocate = false;
 
 		    outrel.r_offset =
 		      _bfd_elf_section_offset (info->output_bfd, info,
@@ -1660,7 +1661,14 @@ microblaze_elf_relocate_section (struct bfd_link_info *info,
 		    if (outrel.r_offset == (bfd_vma) -1)
 		      skip = true;
 		    else if (outrel.r_offset == (bfd_vma) -2)
-		      skip = true;
+		      /* The .eh_frame editor converts this field to a
+			 PC-relative encoding, so no dynamic relocation is
+			 needed, but the absolute value must still be written
+			 into the section for it to compute the delta from.
+			 On this RELA target the addend only exists in the
+			 relocation, so skipping without relocating leaves a
+			 zero behind and the FDE points at address 0.  */
+		      skip = true, relocate = true;
 		    outrel.r_offset += (input_section->output_section->vma
 					+ input_section->output_offset);
 
@@ -1697,6 +1705,10 @@ microblaze_elf_relocate_section (struct bfd_link_info *info,
 		    loc = sreloc->contents;
 		    loc += sreloc->reloc_count++ * sizeof (Elf32_External_Rela);
 		    bfd_elf32_swap_reloca_out (info->output_bfd, &outrel, loc);
+
+		    if (relocate && r_type == R_MICROBLAZE_32)
+		      bfd_put_32 (input_bfd, relocation + addend,
+				  contents + offset);
 		    break;
 		  }
 		else
-- 
